Package: xtop
Version: 0.48.0-1
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Depends: libc6
Recommends: postgresql, journalctl
Installed-Size: 37740
Maintainer: Farhan Tahir <farhan.003@gmail.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/ftahirops/xtop
Description: Incident-first root-cause analysis console for Linux
 v0.48.0 — NEXTGEN architecture milestone. The RCA engine now has
 the structural primitives of an enterprise-grade proof system:
 typed evidence, entity graph, multi-gate verifier with strict
 abstention, and an offline replay corpus.
 .
 Five phases of NEXTGEN_RCA_ARCHITECTURE.md are now in production:
 .
   Phase 1 — Correctness & Stability
     * 3 package-global RCA state pieces removed
     * single finalization point (Engine.finalize)
     * two engines in one process verified isolated by test
 .
   Phase 2 — Typed Fact evidence
     * new model.Fact with 18 fields + provenance
     * 23 typed facts emitted per tick (CPU 6, Memory 7, IO 6,
       Network 4) with per-metric Confidence scores
     * lossless JSON roundtrip — facts are replay-ready
 .
   Phase 3 — Entity graph
     * new model.Entity + model.EntityGraph with O(1) lookup
     * BuildEntityGraph() each tick from process+cgroup tree
     * Fact.EntityID resolves through the graph for ownership
       reasoning
 .
   Phase 4 — Multi-gate verifier with 4-tier output
     * Tier A/B/C/D output with full gate audit trail
     * 5 gates: signal_quality, ownership_consistency,
       temporal_ordering, baseline_deviation, counter_evidence
     * abstain-by-default semantics — engine refuses to commit
       to a strong verdict when proof is weak
 .
   Phase 5 — Replay corpus + measurement harness
     * automatic capture to ~/.xtop/incidents/
     * new xtop replay subcommand with per-mechanism precision
       rollup, single-frame audit, deterministic replay
 .
 18 structural invariants now run on every analysis tick.
 New packages: engine/verifier (5 gate impls + framework),
 engine/replay (offline harness).
 .
 HONEST ABOUT PRECISION: the 0.1% false-positive design target
 from NEXTGEN is now ARCHITECTURALLY ACHIEVABLE but NOT YET
 MEASURED. Architecturally because every primitive is in place;
 not measured because that requires operators to label the captured
 corpus. See docs/NEXTGEN_STATUS.md for full details.
 .
 All v0.47.x features (PHP-FPM diagnostics, Plesk/cPanel multi-pool
 support, ghost-site detection, web-shell scanner with defensive-
 code detection, etc.) remain intact.
